part.text:
We need to add sounds. Likely use HTML5 Audio. We need to add sound effects for collecting debris, collision with asteroid, and maybe background music. We'll create audio objects, load sound files. However we don't have sound files; we can use simple generated beep using Web Audio API? Simpler: use new Audio('path') referencing files that may not exist; but better to use minimal beep via Oscillator.

Implement using Web Audio API: create AudioContext, and functions playBeep(frequency, duration). For collect: play short high beep; for hit: lower beep.

Add in code: create audio context once; define playTone. In update when score increments, call playCollect(); when shield lost, playHit(); when win/lose, play end tone.

We need to add code after canvas init.

Implement in game.js after variables: const audioCtx = new (window.AudioContext || window.webkitAudioContext)(); define function playTone(freq, time) { const osc = audioCtx.createOscillator(); const gain = audioCtx.createGain(); osc.type='sine'; osc.frequency.value=freq; osc.connect(gain); gain.connect(audioCtx.destination); osc.start(); gain.gain.setValueAtTime(0.1, audioCtx.currentTime); osc.stop(audioCtx.currentTime + time); }

Define playCollect =()=>playTone(800,0.1); playHit =()=>playTone(200,0.2); playWin =()=>playTone(1200,0.3); playLose =()=>playTone(150,0.5);

Call accordingly: when score increment, playCollect(); when shield--, playHit(); after game over when loop ends? In draw when gameOver, we could check a flag if not already played; add variable soundPlayed = false; after gameOver set true after playing appropriate sound.

Simplify: In update after setting gameOver true due to score or shield, we could set a variable endReason = 'win'/'lose' then later in draw play once.

Add variables at top: let endReason = null; let endSoundPlayed = false;

When score >= targetScore set gameOver = true; endReason='win'; When shield reaches 0 set gameOver = true; endReason='lose';

In draw, if gameOver && !endSoundPlayed: if endReason==='win' playWin(); else playLose(); endSoundPlayed=true;

Implement edits.

